# Gitignored files copied into each new worktree Claude Code creates.
# Format is .gitignore syntax. Only files that match a pattern AND are
# gitignored are copied, so nothing tracked is ever duplicated.
#
# Why this file exists: a gitignored file normally lives only in the worktree
# where it was created, so machine-local context silently disappears the moment
# work moves to a worktree — which is where most work in this repo happens.
#
# LIMIT, worth knowing before relying on it: this is honoured for worktrees
# CLAUDE CODE creates (`--worktree`, subagent worktrees, desktop parallel
# sessions). A worktree made by hand with `git worktree add` does not get the
# copy; carry the files over yourself, or create the worktree through Claude.

